# Founder design lock (HARD)

Justin Evans owns Athere Mesh / Titan vision and architecture. **Designs are not editable without his express permission in the current message.**

## Forbidden without explicit permission

- Shaving, shrinking, or “simplifying” the intended design so work can be marked done
- Treating incomplete wiring as a redesign (e.g. leaving LOOM/ECHO/Caretaker/Sentinel/clusters unbound and calling that settled)
- Demoting founder agents into `jobs` or dropping them from the usable fleet
- Replacing hot-swappable / full-fleet intent with a thinner static subset
- Renaming established components, inventing parallel architectures, or reinterpreting doctrine to match what is easy to ship
- Claiming READY / done / complete when the deliverable is a reduced version of what he asked for

## Required instead

- Implement toward **his** stated design (full agents, clusters, MEA, proof, mesh loop, hot-swap binding)
- If blocked, say **blocked** with the exact gap — do not redefine success downward
- Ask before changing architecture, roster scope, authority chain, or product thesis
- Prefer unfinished honest state over a shaved “green” story

## Permission test

Only edit design/scope when Justin’s **current** message clearly authorizes that specific change (exact names / exact cut). Prior chats, urgency, or “GET TO WORK” do not grant design edit rights.
